78:| Categoriser | `categorise.py` + `cma/rules/v1.yaml`, `v2.yaml` | Ordered regex rules and name lists, direction-aware, kept as validated data and chosen by `CMA_RULESET`. Precedence: per-line override, protected rules (the line-type cues: returned DD, own-pot moves, HMRC, refunds; then lenders, director, capital introduced, shareholder, generic loan wording), profile names, an ambiguous verdict, firm rules, the rest of the table, the default; each line records its rule id. Under v2 a credit whose matching rules point to two or more money-in buckets (cues first; names only when no cue matches), or that has a payment rail with cash paid-in wording, is ambiguous: it stays `OTHER` (unexplained, never trading receipts) and records `v2:conflict:` with every rule it matched in either stage, the rail included, until a person overrides it or the profile names the payer. Inside one bucket the table's `category_order` picks the category (cash deposit, customer transfer, card settlement; returned payment, refund), never rule order. Names match as whole words in any script. A transfer in is revenue only with an invoice reference. Returned DDs are linked to the debit they undo. Unmatched lines are `OTHER`, never guessed. |
